I've recently switched from a 2-button to a 3-button mouse
(MouseSystems) and had a hard time getting it going. One workaround is
to have X read the mouse from gpm--assuming gpm recognizes it. Check
the -R option in the gpm man page.

I have also managed to use this mouse without gpm by adding the line

     Resolution 420

to the XF86Config file (substitute 420 to whatever makes sense for
your hardware; mine is a 420 dpi). Without it, the cursor resets to
+0-0 every few seconds, making it impossible to use.

HTH,

-Dragos

