Make sure your battery has not puked and died on you.  Mine was shipped to
me with a dead battery and had the exact symptoms you describe.  A new
battery from DALCO Electronics (www.dalco.com) fixed it right up.  If you
have an IDE drive attached, make sure you have the latest firmware version
or it will NOT boot.  Also, you need 36-bit TRUE parity SIMMS, any other
type, including LOGIC parity will not work.

-Ken

