The UX boards from samsung, are to my knowledge only going
to be delivered with the ARC-console.
To run DU erhh Tru64, the SRM-console is needed.
Second, it's claimed that there are two Alpha cores' available,
one for DU, and one for NT, Linux and other OS's.
I don't beleive that this is actually true, but I do beleive that you'll
need to change the SROM in order to make the SRM-console
work.
The cheapest way to get full speed out of the Alpha, that I can think
of, is to use NT with MSVC++ and Digital erhm Compaq
Visual Fortran.
As an alternative, I would check the compilers from Microway,
which supposely should deliver very good performance, but
I've never tried it myself.

Best regards,

Anders Blicher Petersen

