I have the solution.  The problem I ran into was with the boot kernal on the
floppy.  It has a "known bug" according to RedHat and it is not compatible
with any of the NCR SCSI adapters.  I threw a buslogic card in, went through
the install, then powered off before the first reboot and switched
everything to the onboard adapter.  Now it all works great.  Hope this
helps.


