> Got a Multia box running RH 5.2.  Everything works fine, except that I
> can't do anything with the Exabyte.  The system sees the drive from ARC,
> and when booting it recognizes the drive is there:
> 
> kernel: Detected scsi disk sdb at scsi0, channel 0, id 1, lun 0
> kernel:   Vendor: EXABYTE   Model: EXB-85058SQANXR1  Rev: 06M0
> kernel:   Type:   Sequential-Access                  ANSI SCSI revision: 02
> 
> The drive works fine in one of my x86 boxes, but if memory serves when the
> system is done probing the bus, and it has listed the partitions for the
> hard drives, on the x86 box is also lists that it has a st0.  Under the
> Alpha it doesn't.
> 
> I'm guessing that the kernal doesn't support tape drives.

If you have a /proc filesystem, do a `cat /proc/devices'.  Mine says:

	Character devices:
	  1 mem
	  2 pty
	  3 ttyp
	  4 ttyS
	  5 cua
	  6 lp
	  7 vcs
>>>>>>>>  9 st
	 10 misc
	etc.

If you don't have an `st' you probably need to recompile your kernel
(but I thought SCSI support implied SCSI tape?  my memory is fuzzy here.)
If you do have an `st', try going to the /dev directory and doing
an `./MAKEDEV st' as root.

Good luck.



