To install it?  beats me.  To try it out, I ended up copying `milo'
and `ldmilo.exe' to a floppy, having obtained the files from
gatekeeper.dec.com .  I shutdown and reset to the ARC console.
From there, I picked "run a program" and chose ldmilo.exe from 
the floppy (probably as "a:ldmilo.exe", I don't remember the details).
If you have an SRM console, I can't help you.

Neither the original milo nor the one from DEC could boot 2.2.1 from
/dev/sda3.  Even a simple "ls sda3" gets them confused, as if they
were trying to seek past the end of the device.  I thought the point
of milo was to *not* have limitations like that.  Luckily, the kernel
fits on a floppy, with lots of space left.  Both milo's can boot from
there.  (MILO> boot fd:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda3).



