> This is what I am thinking of getting:
> *CPU - 533Mhz 2Mb Cache (21164)
> *Motherboard - UX Series - Onboard NIC & UW SCSI
> *Memory - 64Mb RAM
> *HDD - 4.5Gb IBM UW SCSI
> *CD-ROM - 32x
> *Video - (one that will work with XFree86)
> * Windows NT & Linux (Dual Boot)
> 
> I have a few questions before I decide to buy.
> Sorry if these are stupid questions. :-)

> * Can I use PC PCI Cards (I have a Video
> card which works with XFree86 on my PII)?

Yes

> * From experience does Alpha's performance
> (speed of apps) outweigh Pentium II's?

No

If you use Linux, you get worse performance due to the lack of good
compilers. Although, commercial apps that where compiled with the
Digital Unix compilers exceed PII performance by far.
Compilers will get better in the near future.

> * Can I run 98 software Alpha with NT?

Some. There are (free) Win emulators, however, there is no sound support
yet. Starcraft for instance works.

> * Do all X-Window window managers work on
> Alpha (Window Maker)?

I think so, e, kde and windowmaker (which I consider the three important
ones) do work.

> * Does X-Windows work in SVGA mode?

Yes. But never call it X-windows. It's X, Xfree or maybe W-win. But not
X-windows :)

> * Do Alpha's Support Multiple Video cards
> in NT or even Linux?

? You can use 3d add-on cards, for what it's worth.

> * Because Linux is a 32bit OS and Alpha is 64bit CPU,
> do you get full performance with Linux?

Alpha Linux is 64 bit. *whack* :)

> * I heard that WinNT is 64-bit. Is this so?

Wrong. Alpha NT is 32 bit. NT 5 will be 64 bit, but it is not out yet.

> * Do Alpha Motherboards have USB, RS232, Parallel,
> PS/2 mouse & Keyboard (or large DIN), etc?

No USB, yes to paralell, rs232 and both mouse and key ps/2 (at least
mine has).



Hope I was of some assistance



