> I've heard rumours that the 164LX SRM firmware works on the Samsung UX
> boards, because they're basically LX clones with on-board ethernet and
> SCSI added.

Sadly, no, this is not true. The UX has a different chip-set, it has a PCI-PCI
Bridge and SRM does not exist that can run on UX.

If you need SRM console, then you are limited to the LX and the new DP264 (as
far as current boards go anyway).

