I tried to verify that, but I can't find the difference.
Both EC-R46WB-TE ("AlphaPC 164LX Motherboard Technical Reference Manual")
and Samsung's "AlphaPC 164UX/BX Motherboard Technical Reference Manual"
claim that they use the 21174-CA chipset.

The 21052 PCI-PCI bridge is something that I missed.  But a look into
the LX firmware on the v5.3 CD reveals that it at least knows the
21052's PCI ID and name: 0x1011/0x0021 "DECchip 21052-AA".

So while my hope is fading, I'm still not quite convinced that it's
impossible.

Thank you for pointing out that the LX and UX aren't as similar as I
thought.

joerch



