On Wed, 17 Feb 1999 01:13:50 GMT, wswanson@iso.net wrote:

>4. After the installation completes, install MILO on a small disk partition
>on your machine.  Here is were I am haveing problems. The machine has
>rebooted and is back at the MILO prompt. The root directory does not have
>vmlinux.gz Nor does the msdos partition have MILO. How do I create vmlinux.gz
>with MILO? How do I copy the floppy MILO to the sda1 with MILO. I have tried
>the MILO> run fdo:dd fi=/dev/fdo fo=/dev/sda1 bs=1440k, it fails. Also, I
>have tried several other combinations. Can I create vmlinux on the WIN95
>machine?

Boot up from your kernel floppy again - from the MILO> prompt type
	boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda2
that should get you a login prompt. Login, mount fd0 (that's fdZERO by
the way) thus
	mount /dev/fd0 /mnt
then just
	cp /mnt/vmlinux.gz /
To get MILO on sda1 unmount the kernel floppy and put your MILO disk
in the drive. If necessary run mkdosfs on sda1 to create a DOS
filesystem, then use mcopy to copy milo and linload.exe from the
floppy to sda1.

>The only 2 prompts I can get to on the Alphstation is ARC (firmware 4.57) and
>the MILO. Would someone please be kind enough to give me the information on
>how to get through step 4?

In ARC set up a new boot option similar to the one you set up for
floppy booting but referenceing your hard drive instead. Add an
OSLOADOPTION that contains the MILO boot command 
	boot sda2:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda2
Then when booting all you have to do is hit return in ARC.

Martin



