> know how to switch it manually (or change the detection order)?

The detection can be influenced in the SRM Console. If my memory serves
well, goto UNIX O/S under ARC, and then follow the instruction of the
Multia Handbook, i.e. 

>>>SET EWA0_MODE THIN

then go back to ARC

>>> ARC

and I guess 10base2 will be forced. Didn't try myself, but it's worth
trying.

Standard order of autosensing (with >>>SET EWA0_MODE AUTO) is 10baseT,
10base2 then 10base5.

Peter




