Not sure that you got the installation to work or not, if not try
MILO> boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1
this should boot your floppy-set.

or if you want to boot to linux use
MILO> boot sda2:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda2
 where the 2 in sda2 points to the linux native partition. this will boot
linux for you.

