tried
> the MILO> run fdo:dd fi=/dev/fdo fo=/dev/sda1 bs=1440k, it fails.
This should be done from within linux and not the loader, I believe the
correct syntax to be
dd fi=/dev/fd0 fo=/dev/sda1 bs=1440k
wih the note that fd0 <= is a zero. This copies milo onto your first
partition which should be FAT.
After that you can change the ARC-bootsettings for Milo to be on sda1
instead of fd0

