Hm,
	I just bought one of these, but I also bought the matching
power supply. I havent completed assembling a system yet..

It's a PC64 not a PC164

You need an AT type case. The board is baby AT size. Careful with the
cache chips. They are rather high and my foul the Floppy drive
position. I bought a full tower AT style case. plenty of room in here,
though again the cache is a tight fit. One case I tried would not fit.

The problem is you need an ATX spec Power supply, with the 3.3volt
output. Also the board does not have standard ATX connector s so you
have a bit of fun trying to source these connectors and connect up
correctly.

Get the matching PSU. I t makes life a lot easier. Careful with the
PSU. All four plugs are the same type and not polarized. READ THE
MANUAL carefully.

Any 72 Pin parity SIMM (70ns or better) will do. you need to fit them
in banks of four the same .

I'm gonna stick Linux on mine, when I've got all the bits together.
Apparently they perform quite well

Good luck.

