the cobwebs out of the poor thing. I also inspected everything for signs
of burning and didn't find anything. The computer now starts pretty
reliably and gets me into the ARC console. Now, when I try to install NT
Server, it hangs at various points in formatting the hard drive. I have
3 hard drives and have tried all of them. I've checked my SCSI chain,
changed cables, tried different terminators, tried one drive at a time,
etc. The computer always finds the drives and creates the System
partition with no problem. I am getting the occasional error message
like:

"MACHINE CHECK OCCURRED"
"PC=0x0000000000701b81, VA=0xffffffff808fd038"
"PC=0xffffffff8074f540, VA=0xffffffff808fb188"

and

"PALCODE D-STREAM TB MISS OCCURRED"
"PC=0x0000000000701b8d, VA=0x0000000000000083"

This is pretty much beyond me and I am not sufficiently familiar with
the SRM console to perform the appropriate diagnostics. My best guess is
now something with the memory or the CPU. 

Any light you can shed on this would be much appreciated. Thanks for
responding.

