: My Multia (Alpha AXP-VX40) motherboard just went south. I get power, but
: just a blank screen. Changed the memory, but no improvement. Ergo, I
: believe it's the motherboard. Anyone having a working one that they want
: to part with for a reasonable price, please email.

There is a part that fails on the bottom of the multia motherboard.
It is a surface mount buffer ic, which I do not remember the part 
number of off the top of my head. There is a different (faster/lower
power part) that can be used to replace it. Look on the bottom of the
board for something like a 74F382 and see if it is discolored/cracked
or there is evidence on the motherboard that it is overheating in that
area. 



