Matt Kuznicki (kuznick@bgnet.bgsu.edu) wrote:
: 	Anybody know how to setup an Alpha Multia so that it'll boot from my
: bootp server?  All I've been able to find is "consult your SRM manual"
: for the correct environment variables to set, which didn't come with my
: machine, as I bought it used.

If you indeed run the SRM console, you'll have to figure out the name
of your Ethernet adapter (use "show dev"). Assuming it is "ewa0" and your 
bootp server is on the local network and properly configured, setting 
bootdef_dev to "ewa0", ewa0_inet_init to "bootp", and ewa0_protocols 
to "bootp" should do the trick.

Regards,

/Serge.P



