Danny Chen wrote:
> 
> Ok.
> This is really confusing me.  I have 4 questions:
> 
> 1)  Does the 21164 CPU support the 100 MHz bus speeds?
>         if so, on which motherboards?
No, the 21164 can support buses of any speeds.  It's the supporting
chipset (Alcor, Alcor II, Pyxis) that supports speeds of 33Mhz (for
Alcor and Alcor II) and 66Mhz (Pyxis).
> 
> 2) Does the PC164 Boards take 72 pin SIMMS or DIMM's?
>         What type of DIMMS if DIMMS?
> 
the PC 164 takes SIMMs, 60ns true parity, fast page mode.

> 3) What has to be special and why about the powersupply that connects to a
>     PC164 motherboard?
>
The PC164 uses a custom ATX power supply.  Some of the pins, 13 and 15
(could be wrong) are changed, or something along those lines.  The power
supply is available from Quantum Power Labs (El Paso, TX) or from Axxion
(Also, El Paso, TX).  Also try companies such as http://www.dcginc.com,
they carry the correct power supplies too. 
> 4) What other motherboards support the 21164 CPU?

EB164 (266, 300, 333Mhz) PC164 (300, 333, 366, 400,433, 500Mhz), 164LX
(466, 533, 600, 667, 733, 800 Mhz), 164UX (333Mhz thru 800Mhz designed
by Deskstation Technologies, aka "Ruffian".  The EB164 and PC164 use ARC
bios.  The 164LX uses the Alpha Bios, the Ruffian uses ARCS Bios.  

I hope this helps!

