I'm running an AS200 using the SCM Swapbox that I got from ONSALE.  After a
few false starts and some help from David Hines (plus fully reading the
PCMCIA-HOWTO) PCMCIA card services work!

I started with Redhat Alpha 5.1, kernel 2.0.35 and have since moved up to RH
5.2 and upgraded to kernel 2.0.36.

I used a PCMCIA-CS-3.0.6 pre-release from October.  The pre-release I used
was pcmcia-cs-24-oct-98.tar.gz

In the /etc/sysconfig/pcmcia file I modified PCIC_OPTS to read:
PCIC_OPTS="irq_list=5,14"

These were two IRQ's I knew were not in use.  Without limiting the IRQ range
I experienced lockups when the card services searched for available IRQ's.
When the search hit IRQ 11 for the NCR 810 SCSI controller my drives would
time out and the system would be unusable.

I have tried to upgrade to the regular release of PCMCIA-CS-3.0.6 and 3.0.7,
but a change in the memory include ranges prevents the pc card modem I have
from working.  So I just stay with what I know works and haven't had a
problem.

I would believe that the card services would work on your Multia.  If you
need the PCMCIA support, try it out.  David Hines responded to my message on
support quite quickly from the Dejanew pcmcia forum.

Dennis Connolly

