> 

I have found this to be true, and the crux of the difficulty at 
installing RedHat to a Jensen.

> I have read all the documents on the net about how to install on the Jensen,
> and getting RH 5.1 to start installation is "no" problem.
> I have even tried to switch to bsd style format in fdisk, but RH 5.1 does
> not seem to find the partitions anyway.
> 

That was also my experience. I ended up playing with both the fdisk and 
bsd style partition tables during the installation to get around this. I 
boot the installation with the minlabel/copyboot created drive, knowing 
precisely what the contents of the partition table. I created identical 
partitions at the fdisk point in the RedHat installation, and then before 
shutting down I revisited the partition table in a separate virtual 
console, using fdisk and swriteboot to fiddle with the aboot kernel (0/a) 
and the partition tables. I don't remember the details of this fiddling, 
so if you try to share a drive between aboot/linux, take good notes to 
better help the next person in need.

> Is this a RH 5.1 problem, and will it go away if i get RH 5.2 or am I doing
> something wrong ?
> 

My experience was with RedHat 5.2, so I think the answer is no, it won't 
go away and yes, there is something wrong. What's wrong? Is it the tools 
in the RedHat installation that don't recognize the BSD partitions? Or is 
it the kernel that is boot for the installation that doesn't recognize 
the BSD partitions? 

I don't know. Does anyone?

Again. Good luck.


