My Experience:

I got my alpha MB + Proc from HardData  They can also be sourced from a
distributor  such as Jaco (http://www.jacoelectronics.com) - but I found that
HardData in canada had better than wholesale prices - go figure!  One Hint -
when they say Cheque he means MONEY ORDER or Cashiers Check!  (My check took
40 days to process... talk about gut wrenching!)

I got an Axxion DL-17 case from my local vendor with
300W PS.  Make sure the back drive bay is in the case.... mine was missing?
(http://www.swtechnology.com) If my PSU blows I want to have
someone local.  (This being a very failure-prone part on all syss IMHO.)

The memory I ordered was off the internet  Dynasty Express sold me 128 MB
for 206.97.  (A great price at the time)  More importantly, it worked like a
champ.  The actual Part was 8X72S7ECC-GOL (64MB 8x72 PC100 ECC 7ns).
One thing I picked up is that ECC PC100 is by definition unbuffered.  (PC100 is
still confusing in my mind)  (http://www.dynastyexpress.com)  They were also
the first to delive, on time and right so they were good to me!  (They are also
listed on www.PriceWatch.com)

KB, Mouse, HD and Ethernet were all standard.

Good Luck!

