There are 2?!? problems here. One is that the hardware includes
things like cables. I found that the headers on the axppci33 do
not conform to the "standard" PC pinout. Not a major problem, and
relatively easy to fix, but a royal pain to discover for an x86
old timer(with lots of spare PC parts) who's becoming an alpha newbie.

Ah, it's been a while now, but I recall something about cua/ttyS0
being the default console port. Try attaching the mouse to the
second port. Other than that, ignore the mouse config utils. I've
never seen a RedHat release in which they worked. From installation
on they always want to install a ps2 on psaux(yes, even when no
mouse is attached to anything) and I always tell them that I've got
a serial, 3 button generic on the second port. Everything works fine.




