Yeah, the G3 is kind of bad at FP. They went all out on integer, cutting
out the second FP unit that the 604 had that gave it an FP advantage over
the PII. Altivec (The PPC's answer to KNI that looks like it may make KNI
look like a joke is we can trust the numbers coming out of Motorola) on
the G4 (now in "beta") should allow (Motorola sources claim) the G4 to be
*4x* as fast as the G3 on FP. There are some benchmarks based on
unofficial Motorola numbers at
http://www.appleinsider.com/articles/9902/images/altivec-vs-max.gif and an
article on the architecture (more technical info is easy to find at
Motorola's web site) at
http://www.appleinsider.com/articles/9902/altivec-g4.shtml

