Maxx Christopher Lobo wrote in message <36B683AA.42494E79@maxx.ml.org>...
>Guys---
>Having compiled the kernel, all is rosy... with one exception:
>windowmaker will not run! It gives me a
>
>windowmaker fatal error: could not open display ""


How are you logging onto this machine? Console, telnet, ssh etc...

It looks like you display is not getting exported properly.
If your at the console try

    export DISPLAY=:0.0 (for bash etc, or setenv DISPLAY :0.0 for csh).

If you are logging in from another machine does that other machine have an
X-server
running? If this is the case you'll need to export the display to the other
machine.
Something like...

        export DISPLAY=othermachine:0.0

        -where othermachine is the name or I.P. of you other machine.

Make sense?


