you need three disks

MILO, BOOT, and ROOT
MILO is from \milo\images\udb-noname.img
BOOT is the \images\noname.img
ROOT is your ramdisk.img

Put in the MILO disk, set your UDB to boot from floppy

after you got into the milo prompt
incert your boot disk and type:
 boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

after it reads the kernel, it will ask you to put in the
ROOT disk.

then you are on your way.


